WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.830
He's not here.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:49.420
On to the next one!

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:54.280
<b>Sarabaka</b>

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:00.000
<i>This presence...</i>

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.290
<i>Something...</i>

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.490
<i>is coming closer.</i>

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:11.710
Building 5 is so quiet, it's creepy.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.230
All the surveillance systems around 
the Gogyousan area are cut off,

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:18.510
and there's no response from Hajime and Kiji.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.690
This is seriously bad, no?

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.490
I guess this proves that guy really did escape.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.310
This might just be the worst 
crisis in Nanba Prison's history.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:32.300
Maybe I should alert the entire prison?

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.900
Wait just a moment.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:34.530
Huh?

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.150
There should be a reason.

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:41.740
Reason for escaping? Enki killed an inmate.

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:48.720
Even now, I don't think what Enki-san 
did that day was just a murder.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.840
What is the reason, then?

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:56.650
He doesn't share what's 
on his mind with anyone.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.640
What's on his mind, huh?

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.760
I wonder what the heck 
is going on right now.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:11.650
Hold it right there!

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.540
You made a mess of the underground prison!

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:15.910
How much do you think it's 
gonna cost to fix all this?!

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:17.750
Well? Is it close?

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:20.210
Yeah, we should be just about there.

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:22.160
Then let's do it!

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.180
You piece of...

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:30.580
Move this damn thing!

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:33.470
You'd better pay for the damage to the floor!

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:33.470
This should hold them for a while.

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:35.590
Trois, you'd better not mess this up.

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:38.720
Not a chance. I'm not you, Honey-kun.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.050
What was that?!

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.690
<i>As expected, it's hard to see.</i>

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:49.070
<i>Whoa!</i>

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.930
<i>You're going to challenge me in the water?</i>

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:58.140
<i>Okay... Come and get me.</i>

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:05.410
Hakkai, what's the meaning of this?

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:06.880
Aw, man...

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.800
It looks like they've escaped.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.670
I had guards stationed here just in case,

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:14.830
but I didn't expect them to escape.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:32.510
I shouldn't have skipped out 
on Yamato's exercise sessions.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:39.860
Where are you going? That way is...

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.700
I know.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:54.420
<i>Fooled you!</i>

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:00.600
<i>I don't really want to use this on a man,</i>

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:02.000
<i>but I guess I'll have to.</i>

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:06.410
<i>Allow me to explain!</i>

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:09.230
<i>When Inmate Number 3 wants 
to compliment a woman,</i>

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:14.530
<i>he is able to emit this aura with just 
a smile, without saying a word!</i>

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:16.360
<i>It'll make any woman swoon.</i>

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:19.060
<i>You're looking very beautiful today.</i>

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.530
<i>Oh!</i>

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:25.490
<i>By the way, this aura is made from 100% 
natural handsomeness-derived components!</i>

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:27.790
<i>Oh, </i>Nanbaka<i>...</i>

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:30.230
<i>Oh? This one gets it.</i>

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:34.240
<i>And why is it working on this guy, 
even though he's not a woman?! Why?!</i>

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:37.500
<i>That answer lies within your heart.</i>

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.040
<i>Let's meet again some day!</i>

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.940
<i>I took extra care with my makeup today,</i>

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:43.170
<i>so I guess he can't help but notice.</i>

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:48.770
<i>Water doesn't affect my latest 
waterproof mascara at all. I love it!</i>

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:49.560
<i>Here it is.</i>

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:54.600
<i>I never thought my technique for flattering 
Kiji-san would come in handy here.</i>

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.020
Gotcha!

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.860
See? What did I tell you?

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:04.470
How did you know that kappa was carrying it?

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:09.360
Those two are at each other's throats all 
the time, so if one of them is imprisoned,

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:11.470
the other will want to dangle 
the keys in front of him.

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:15.210
Besides, the egotistical 
guards crave authority,

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:18.720
so they're the ones most likely 
to be carrying the keys.

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:20.400
Come to think of it...

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.150
If Trois was imprisoned alone,

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:23.870
I'd definitely do that, too.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:25.940
That's Building 5 for you!

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:26.880
These two!

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.390
Damn you punks!

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:30.770
How strong are their fists?!

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:30.770
They're not human!

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:32.100
Hold it right there!

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:35.880
Darn it!

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:39.140
No matter how much I polish these 
bars, I can't see my reflection!

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:41.560
I'm really worried about how 
my makeup looks right now.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:43.360
What?

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:47.420
There he is!

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:48.950
Why are you guys crying?!

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.940
And what are you even doing here?!

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:52.900
How are you running around freely?

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:53.830
What's going on?

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:56.040
We'll explain the details later!

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.160
You're not getting away!

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.120
Youriki and Kokoriki?!

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.710
They're attacking from 
the front, like I said!

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:03.610
I know! If this plan doesn't 
go as you said,

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:04.960
you're gonna get it!

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:05.760
That won't...

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:06.670
...even hit us!

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:10.930
The center is wide open... Huh?

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:14.260
Oh, crap!

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:20.130
By the way, what you did just 
now counts as an offense, too.

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:21.190
Prepare yourselves.

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:23.520
You stupid guards!

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:24.820
What?!

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:29.530
What is the meaning of this?

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:33.910
You two have some nerve 
to lock me up in here.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:39.920
N-No, we were just trying to apprehend 
the escaped convicts, and...

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:45.550
Ruka is an inmate in the underground prison!

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:48.480
You should've been told that he should 
be handled with extreme caution!

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:51.250
If you have the time to catch petty inmates,

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:52.850
you should capture Ruka first!

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:54.050
Petty...

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:56.600
Go look at the condition of Building 5, now!

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.020
Y-Yes, sir.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:00.340
Jeez...

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:03.460
I need to tell that monkey to have a 
refresher course for his inmates.

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:04.930
<i>S-Scary...</i>

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:06.500
<i>But we're saved.</i>

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:07.780
You two are next!

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:09.700
We're not saved!

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:12.700
<b>Please Stand By</b>

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:17.280
Well, you got me out, 
so I guess that'll do for now.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:18.330
Say you're sorry!

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:19.770
We're sorry.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:22.050
<i>Scary...</i>

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:24.120
Anyway, where's Number 3?

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:32.300
No!

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:33.320
What are you doing?!

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:34.840
This outfit is brand new!

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:38.190
I'll have to get this dry cleaned again!

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:41.390
Uh, Kiji-san, I can get out myself.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:45.520
This looks like the work of Ruka's Bashosen.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:49.790
You guys aren't injured, are you? 
Any scratches? Bruises?

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:51.110
No, not really.

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:52.860
Just lost a little blood.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:54.650
Be careful, will you?!

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:57.490
The fan club's visiting for a tour next week!

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:59.500
You can't get sick or injured!

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.900
For crying out loud, don't worry me like that!

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:03.710
Um... What about me?

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.490
Why should I be worried about an outsider?!

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:07.240
Damn it! Good point!

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:11.300
Wh-What the...

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:15.800
Why, you! How dare you 
steal the keys from me?!

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:16.300
Huh?

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:19.470
Oh, my. If it isn't Ruka.

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:21.350
K-Kiji! How?!

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:22.550
Here.

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:23.540
What?

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:27.230
Give me my hand mirror and Bashosen, too.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:29.610
Try and take them by force!

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:32.750
Very well, I'll just do that, then.

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:34.110
Especially my hand mirror!

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:35.070
You want <i>that</i> more?!

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:37.420
I'm gonna blow you away!

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:39.480
Isn't this bad?

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:40.960
Don't worry.

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:44.370
Ruka... What is it that 
you're planning to do here?

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:48.670
It's nothing you would ever understand!

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:53.420
Hmph! You sound just like Enki.

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:57.510
You won't get closer to him 
just by acting like him.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:00.100
Are you saying I can't strive 
to be like Enki-san?!

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:04.320
I worked hard and came this 
far to get closer to him!

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:06.170
I was supposed to be the deputy supervisor,

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:09.040
not that worthless little brother of his!

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:10.660
Me! Ruka Gojyou!

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:13.860
He's always on the right path!

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:17.110
So you're saying killing 
someone is righteous?!

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:18.580
Of course I am!

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:21.480
If killing is the way to get closer to him,

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:23.320
I'll gladly do it!

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:40.980
The thing you're trying to get closer to...

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:44.070
is much too big... and dangerous!

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.400
Before you try to be like someone,

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:51.120
you should reexamine yourself first.

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:59.860
I... I just...

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:04.120
Huh?

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:07.870
Your makeup is ruined.

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:08.920
Huh? Seriously?!

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:12.100
No! My latest waterproof mascara!

00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:14.160
Like I said before, that's my mirror!

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:14.870
No!

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:15.840
Supervisor Mitsuba!

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:18.800
We apologize, but this hallway is blocked.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:19.980
I see.

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:23.260
Then let's exit above 
by using the back way.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:29.730
<b>Gogyousan
Underground
Level 5</b>

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:52.000
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:57.010
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:04.760
Hey, monkey.

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:06.100
What?

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:09.040
I don't know what Enki is thinking,

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:10.770
but he did escape.

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:13.050
I'm sick of being here.

00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:15.020
If you're not going, I will.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:16.770
Are you stupid?!

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:20.120
You know what'll happen if you 
try to remove those handcuffs!

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:22.160
You want your limbs to get blown off?!

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:24.780
My limbs? Who cares about those?

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:25.630
What?

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:30.300
I don't have time to sit around all day.

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:32.920
I came here to work.

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:38.420
Sitting here just because I want to keep 
my limbs is nothing but humiliating.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:40.920
Are you serious?

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:43.430
More than you are.

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:48.530
Dim-witted monkey... Just watch.

00:11:58.220 --> 00:12:01.070
Hajime and the monkey are 
on the fifth level, right?

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:03.210
You put those handcuffs on them, too?

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:07.120
Inori did. He's the one who brought them.

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:08.310
I see.

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:10.130
Once I take you guys outside,

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:13.570
I'll go to the fifth level and bring 
those two idiots back myself.

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:15.860
You guys stay with Youriki in the meantime.

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:17.000
Yes, sir.

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:18.510
Which reminds me...

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:22.730
Number 69 is in the infirmary, and 
Number 25 is on the first underground level.

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:25.140
Wasn't there one more from Cell 13?

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:27.890
You let him escape?!

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:29.680
Why didn't you tell me that earlier?!

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:32.210
Sorry, sorry, sorry!

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:39.400
<i>That boy does have superhuman power, 
like Number 634 from Building 4.</i>

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:42.070
<i>But even so...</i>

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:46.030
<i>To think he was able to escape the 
Gogyousan underground prison so easily...</i>

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:54.820
<i>If he's more than we expected...</i>

00:12:54.820 --> 00:12:57.880
<i>If he exceeds the data
in our reports about him...</i>

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:00.560
<i>It could get a little dangerous.</i>

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:03.880
He's...

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:09.640
Why are you trying to 
do something so stupid?

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:12.640
We're all in trouble if you do that.

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:17.020
I finally found you, Hajime.

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:21.090
You really put me through hell, you know.

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:22.280
Number 15...

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:25.230
Why are you here?

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:29.160
Huh?

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:35.930
It's awfully quiet.

00:13:35.930 --> 00:13:37.980
Where did Liang and the others go?

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:39.800
Maybe they died?

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:42.750
Damn! There are more?!

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.750
Ow!

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:44.380
Liang!

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:45.290
Uno?

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:48.320
I told you there weren't any 
more surveillance dolls.

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:50.610
You don't listen, do you?

00:13:50.610 --> 00:13:52.310
It's Uno-kun!

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:55.140
Why are Kokoriki-san and 
Youriki-san here, too?

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:57.880
Nico, are you okay? What about your medicine?

00:13:57.880 --> 00:13:59.880
Sorry, but I'm fine now!

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:01.900
The old man gave me my medicine.

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:03.290
Rokuriki?!

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:04.900
He's just unconscious.

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:08.740
Oh? You weren't with us earlier,
were you, old man?

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:09.410
Well...

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:12.850
It's a long story, but he 
joined us along the way.

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:15.790
Yes. Uh, Upa-san, please don't 
punch my stomach. It hurts.

00:14:16.090 --> 00:14:17.200
All right, all right.

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:19.920
Line up, inmates. 
You're going to get handcuffed.

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:24.420
Hey...

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:25.280
Hmm?

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:27.170
Where are Jyugo-kun and Hajime-chan?

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:28.950
Well...

00:14:30.990 --> 00:14:33.560
They should be fine now.

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:37.000
Ow! Hey, what's the idea?

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:43.150
It's them!

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:46.370
Who was it that said there were 
no more surveillance dolls?

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:49.970
This is why your stories are untrustworthy.

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:50.700
Please don't kick me. It hurts.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.700
You guys are increasing my workload.

00:14:55.930 --> 00:14:57.200
For crying out loud!

00:14:58.150 --> 00:14:59.910
This is the underground prison.

00:14:59.910 --> 00:15:03.220
It's not a place where inmates 
can roam around freely.

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:05.980
Yet you came alone all the 
way to the lowest level,

00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:09.720
where there's no exit. It makes no sense.

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:12.470
What are you planning this time?

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.710
Depending on the reason, I'll...

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:17.100
Shut up.

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:19.850
I...

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:23.140
I came here of my own will!

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:28.220
They said there are things only I can do.

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:31.110
Things I can only do because I'm me.

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:39.120
I've been thinking for a long time about 
what I can do and what I'm here for.

00:15:39.650 --> 00:15:41.790
But I couldn't find the answer.

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:44.690
I started to feel afraid 
of others and myself.

00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:48.250
And I thought, maybe they're 
better off without me.

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:51.980
I once thought seriously about escaping.

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:54.580
But the truth is...

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:59.620
I just didn't want people to hate me.

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:02.190
I was so afraid of that, 
I tried running away again.

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:03.730
But...

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:08.780
I realized this about 
myself because of them.

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:14.490
So I decided that I wouldn't be afraid.

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:21.420
I will accept everything about 
myself, both past and future,

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:22.490
and live.

00:16:23.760 --> 00:16:26.600
I'm going to start my life all over again.

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:30.170
I'm not empty anymore!

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:34.010
That's why I can't just stay put forever!

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:47.400
In the first place...

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:51.100
I went through all this trouble 
because you got caught so easily!

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:53.650
What's more, the former Building 
5 supervisor has escaped,

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:55.440
and there are creepy-looking jiangshis!

00:16:55.440 --> 00:16:58.500
So I came all the way here 
to rescue you guards!

00:16:58.500 --> 00:16:59.940
Why are <i>you</i> getting angry?

00:16:59.940 --> 00:17:01.660
If you want to be rescued, just say so!

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:03.420
You're saying that to me?!

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:05.590
You're the one in the cell!

00:17:08.740 --> 00:17:12.620
<i>Crap... I didn't know he 
was in the same place.</i>

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:17.330
<i>Hajime has been hiding the fact 
that I can easily escape.</i>

00:17:17.330 --> 00:17:19.270
<i>If I easily unlock the door here...</i>

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:19.940
Hey!

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:21.860
Hurry up and open it!

00:17:21.860 --> 00:17:23.380
Uh, but if I do that...

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:25.380
Shut up. It's already too late.

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:27.810
Huh? Don't say I didn't warn you.

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:37.040
What are you looking at?!

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:39.970
It's refreshing to see you in handcuffs.

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:41.920
Uno and the rest would 
laugh their heads off.

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:42.950
Shut up!

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:46.320
Crap!

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:47.790
Hurry up and remove these, too!

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:57.130
Seriously?

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:57.830
Let's go.

00:17:58.200 --> 00:17:59.800
What about him?

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:01.550
Go.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:03.540
You heard him. Let's go.

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:06.430
But Liang asked me to save him, too.

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:08.060
Number 2 did?

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:10.040
Besides, if you leave the cell alone,

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:12.320
won't it make things complicated?

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:13.400
<i>He's right.</i>

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:17.450
<i>True, it wouldn't look good if I got 
out and he remained underground.</i>

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:20.480
<i>If they find out I was
the only one to escape,</i>

00:18:20.480 --> 00:18:24.520
<i>it'll probably make Number 15's
jailbreaking look even worse.</i>

00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:27.300
<i>If they start thinking I 
used an inmate to escape,</i>

00:18:27.300 --> 00:18:29.660
<i>that'll be more than just a 
blemish on my reputation.</i>

00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:30.940
<i>If that happens...</i>

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:33.410
<i>No, but it'll still interfere with 
my duties from here on out.</i>

00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:35.920
<i>Kiji will probably nag me about it, as well.</i>

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:37.590
<i>More importantly, I can't let the warden—</i>

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:38.830
Hurry it up!

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:40.020
No choice, I guess.

00:18:40.020 --> 00:18:41.340
It's an emergency. Let him out.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:44.720
No one asked you...

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:46.990
You never shut up, do you, monkey?

00:18:46.990 --> 00:18:48.480
I'm telling you to get back to work.

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:50.820
What did you say?! Hajime, you—

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:57.110
Uh... You did want them removed, right?

00:19:02.060 --> 00:19:07.120
Hajime! I knew you were hiding 
the fact that this guy can escape!

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:08.580
You knew everything!

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:10.740
Do you know what this means?!

00:19:10.740 --> 00:19:13.810
It means you endorsed an inmate's escape!

00:19:13.810 --> 00:19:16.340
You think you can get away with—

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:22.760
Once you're free, you're instantly annoying.

00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:26.300
Never mind. He's obnoxious.

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:29.240
Let's just lock him in here again.

00:19:29.240 --> 00:19:31.360
<i>He's evil.</i>

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:36.420
Whoa...

00:19:36.420 --> 00:19:38.970
We need to get rid of them to move ahead.

00:19:41.190 --> 00:19:43.240
You'd better not slow me down.

00:19:43.520 --> 00:19:45.280
You're a guard, aren't you?

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:47.130
You'd better protect me.

00:20:13.830 --> 00:20:16.860
The demon makes his appearance.

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:03.530
<b>Nanbaka</b>
